    "body": "### Problem\n\nRaising a float's zindex with `nvim_win_set_config()` after it has been drawn doesn't result in it getting displayed on top of a float with a lower zindex.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate `example.lua`.\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'FloatA', {\n  ctermfg = 'Black', ctermbg = 'LightYellow', fg = 'Black', bg = 'LightYellow',\n})\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'FloatB', {\n  ctermfg = 'Black', ctermbg = 'LightRed', fg = 'Black', bg = 'LightPink',\n})\n\nlocal function float(text, row, col, hl)\n  local buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(false, true)\n  local line = text:rep(3)\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, {line, line, line})\n  local win = vim.api.nvim_open_win(buf, false, {\n    relative = 'editor', row = row, col = col, width = 3, height = 3, style = 'minimal', zindex = 40\n  })\n  vim.wo[win].winhighlight = 'NormalFloat:' .. hl\n  return win\nend\n\nfloat('A', 2, 4, 'FloatA')\nlocal b = float('B', 3, 5, 'FloatB')\nvim.cmd('redraw')\n\nvim.api.nvim_win_set_config(b, {zindex = 41})\nvim.cmd('redraw')\n```\n\nThen source the file.\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n:source example.lua\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpected: the B window has a higher zindex than the A window and should be shown on top.\n\nActual: The A window is shown on top of the B window.\n\n<img width=\"648\" height=\"526\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52a66d8b-992e-4aba-aaf1-3e642b4a71c2\" />\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1952+g187d13aa60 (nightly)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 27.0.1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nTerminal.app 2.15\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nNightly tar",
